- term:
    id: GO:0031663
    label: lipopolysaccharide-mediated signaling pathway
  evidence_type: IEA
  original_reference_id: GO_REF:0000108
  qualifier: involved_in
  supporting_entities:
  - GO:0001875
  review:
    summary: Electronic inference (GO_REF:0000108) from the LPS immune receptor activity annotation.
    action: REMOVE
    reason: Derived mechanically from GO:0001875, which is not supported for TLR6 (TLR6-deficient cells lose responses only to diacylated lipopeptide; LPS is sensed by TLR4:MD-2). TLR6 is not a component of the LPS signaling pathway.
    supported_by:
    - reference_id: PMID:11431423
      supporting_text: Here we show that TLR6-deficient (TLR6(-/-)) cells are unresponsive to MALP-2 but retain their normal responses to lipopeptides of other bacterial origins.
