  review:
    summary: Crystal structure of the TLR6 TIR domain reveals homodimer interfaces.
    action: KEEP_AS_NON_CORE
    reason: Homodimer inferred from crystal packing of the isolated TIR domain; physiological role unclear (TLR6 functions as a heterodimer with TLR2 or TLR4).
    supported_by:
    - reference_id: PMID:25088687
      supporting_text: Our structure reveals novel homo-dimerization interfaces, which might be a critical for the interaction with TIR-containing adaptor proteins and itself.
